Rule 11 (index tensor (v_3) is within the input tensor along the specified dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= min(v_3) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_3) ≤ shape(v_1, v_2) − 1

Rule 26 (tuple of ints used as kernel size must have length 2)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] > 0

Rule 3 (input tensors must have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)

Rule 15 (broadcasting compatibility for tensor shapes)
